# Local inputs for the workbench in `.notebooks/`: corpora, `.sds` directories,
# CSVs, checkpoints -- whatever a feature needs to be exercised against real
# data rather than a fixture.
#
# Deny-by-default, like the four import policies under `.scratch/`: nothing here
# is tracked unless it is named below. Everything you put in this directory is
# ignored, and here that is a stronger claim than convenience. Data is usually
# large, and it is often *not ours to vendor* -- `.scratch/dl/`'s policy turns
# away MelodyHPO's `data/` for exactly that reason, since it is a checkout of a
# separate repository. Record provenance in README.md instead of committing the
# bytes.
#
# The policy lives *here* rather than as a `/.data/` line in the repo-root
# `.gitignore`: a directory ignored at the root is one git never descends into,
# so a nested `.gitignore` would never be consulted, and the directory could not
# survive a clone -- git tracks no empty directories.
#
# The repo-root `.gitignore` still applies underneath these rules. The leading
# dot matches pytest's default `norecursedirs` entry `.*`, and the directory
# sits outside `packages/`, so neither the test run nor the workspace glob
# `packages/*` ever looks in here.
#
# Nothing in any distribution may read from this directory. A test or a module
# under `packages/` that reaches in here passes locally and fails everywhere
# else, because this content exists on one machine only. That is the same rule
# `.scratch/README.md` states for imported source, and it applies with more
# force to data that was never tracked at all.

# --- deny everything at this level -------------------------------------------
*

# The policy itself, and our own writing -- chiefly the provenance notes in
# README.md. This negation is easy to forget and fails silently: a file written
# here without it is simply invisible to `git status`, so work looks committed
# and is not. That failure mode has caught out three of the four `.scratch/`
# imports -- see
# `docs/design/adr/0014-scratch-retention-and-per-package-scoping.md`.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
